ain fatty acids</article-title><source>Biotechnol Prog</source><year>2004</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>1015</fpage><lpage>1024</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15296425</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/bp034380e</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gottschalk</surname><given-names/></name></person-group><source>Bacterial metabolism</source><year>1986</year><edition>Second</edition><publisher-name>New York: Springer-Verlag</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Filipe</surname><given-names>CDM</given-names></name><name><surname>Daigger</surname><given-names>GT</given-names></name><name><surname>Grady</surname><given-names>CPL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A metabolic model for acetate uptake under anaerobic conditions by glycogen accumulating organisms: Stoichiometry, kinetics, and the effect of pH</article-title><source>Biotechnol Bioeng</source><year>2001</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11400103</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/bit.1022</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gommers</surname><given-names>PJF</given-names></name><name><surname>Vanschie</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Vandijken</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuenen</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biochemical Limits to Microbial-Growth Yields &#x02013; an Analysis of Mixed Substrate Utilization</article-title><source>Biotechnol Bioeng</source><year>1988</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>86</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18584721</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/bit.260320112</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B2